Defect F2 (pipe): BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipe crashes the process when the sweep of a
face profile fails on part of the spine.

Defect id: F2 (pySMESH phase 4, finding F2, brief amendment 4).

Symptom: a spine that is a degree-4 Bezier curve through the poles
(-0.845, -0.984, -0.652), (-3.252, -3.050, 1.382), (1.781, 0.093, -7.257),
(-2.439, -2.658, 0.313), (-1.140, -0.689, -1.099), and a profile that is a planar
0.077 x 1 rectangle face at the origin. The BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipe constructor
reads address 0x38 and the process ends with an access violation. A straight
spine with the same face builds.

Root cause: BRepFill_Pipe::MakeShape(), face profile. Each wire of the face is swept by
BRepFill_Sweep, and the sweep's SubShape() array becomes myFaces
(BRepFill_Pipe.cxx:696-715 at V8_0_1). The sweep is not asked whether it is done; here
it is not (BRepFill_Sweep::IsDone() false, measured). Where it built no face the array
holds a null shape. The loop that collects the faces of the solid then calls
myFaces->Value(ii, jj).ShapeType() (line 809), which reads the TShape of the null shape;
the IsNull() test on the next lines comes too late.

Change: a null entry of myFaces in that loop throws StdFail_NotDone. The solid
cannot be closed without the face, so the pipe fails at the face it lacks.
BRepFill_Pipe already reports a profile it cannot sweep by throwing
(Standard_DomainError, line 614). Kind: a clean failure, not a computed pipe:
the sweep has no face to give for that part of the spine. Only an input that
read the null shape reaches the throw.

Files and functions changed:
  src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBool/BRepFill/BRepFill_Pipe.cxx
    BRepFill_Pipe::MakeShape(), face branch, the loop over myFaces.

Applies to: OCCT V8_0_1 (b8f597c677811d1f9f4d8a97f5ae2825c0353a42), after 0001.

